1280:### Run-Level Compaction Activity
1281:
1282:Compaction lifecycle state keeps the latest status on `AgentRunState`, but the
1283:visible history is projected through `AgentActivityStore` as `CompactionActivity`
1284:rows.
1285:
1286:- Backend/runtime phases are `requested`, `started`, `completed`, and `failed`; provider-native statuses such as `compacting` and `compacted` are normalized by `compactionActivityProjection.ts`.
1287:- `handleCompactionStatus` delegates to the compaction projection, stores the latest status on `context.state.compactionStatus`, and upserts a `kind: 'compaction'` activity row.
1288:- AutoByteus semantic compaction uses backend-owned `compaction_operation_id` as the parent Activity identity across deferred lifecycle states. A request may be queued on one turn and executed on a later turn; `requested_turn_id` and `execution_turn_id` are lifecycle metadata, while child `compaction_run_id` and `compaction_task_id` enrich the same row instead of replacing its identity.
1289:- Provider-native compaction boundaries remain a separate identity family from AutoByteus semantic compaction operations, so provider boundary keys/operation ids do not collide with backend-owned semantic `compaction_operation_id` rows.
1290:- `AgentEventMonitor` receives an explicit run identity from single-agent, focused team-member, and mobile chat shells, sources compaction activities by that `state.runId`, and passes them to `AgentConversationFeed`, which renders `CompactionStatusRow` inside the scrollable event feed. This avoids using display conversation ids such as `teamRunId::routeKey` as activity-store keys.
1291:- Frontend compaction rows animate the arrow-path/sync icon only for the active `started` phase using motion-safe animation classes; queued, completed, and failed states stay visually still.
1292:- Historical/reopen compaction rows come from durable run projection activity entries, including available `provider_compaction_boundary` traces and AutoByteus semantic compaction events carrying stable operation identity; the frontend does not fabricate rows from latest status alone.
1293:- Failure details stay visible in compaction rows, while detailed token-budget numbers remain in server/runtime logs instead of a live frontend debug panel.
