1297:## Error Event Nuance (Tool vs System)
1298:
1299:The backend can emit:
1300:
1301:- Explicit tool terminal lifecycle events (`TOOL_EXECUTION_FAILED`, `TOOL_DENIED`) for invocation-scoped failures.
1302:- A generic `ERROR` event for visible runtime/turn failures and diagnostics.
1303:  Additive `error_scope`, `error_effect`, and conditional `turn_id` fields
1304:  distinguish turn diagnostics from matching turn-terminal and runtime-terminal
1305:  evidence; an unclassified error has no lifecycle authority.
1306:- Explicit turn-scoped lifecycle events (`TURN_STARTED`, `TURN_COMPLETED`,
1307:  `TURN_INTERRUPTED`) for one accepted user turn.
1308:
1309:`AGENT_STATUS` is run-scoped or exact team-member state.
1310:`TEAM_RUN_LIFECYCLE` is only the root team active/inactive fact.
1311:`TURN_COMPLETED` is the preferred signal when a client needs to know that one
1312:exact turn has finished. Correlate terminal boundaries
1313:and turn-scoped errors by `turn_id`; delayed events for turn A must not settle a
1314:newer turn B. Ordinary segment/tool/inter-agent/todo/system-task activity is
1315:content/progress only and must not infer `running` or recover/reopen a terminal
1316:turn.
1317:
1318:`TOOL_LOG` is diagnostic-only and never the lifecycle authority for completion/failure.
